I replaced the member-wise copy (which forces an out-of-line `FieldBase` copy-constructor call plus several scalar stores) with a single inlined `memcpy` of the whole trivially-copyable object, cutting the copy down to a couple of vector moves.

```include
#include <cstring>
```

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
{
    std::memcpy(static_cast<void *>(this), static_cast<const void *>(&field), sizeof(Field));
}
```